        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink leading-tight mb-4">
          Is a Car Accident Settlement Taxable? What You Need to Know in 2026
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed mb-2">
          By <strong>FreeInjuryCalc Editorial Team</strong> &bull; Reviewed by <strong>Sarah Jenkins, Esq.</strong>
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Table of Contents -->
      <nav class="p-5 border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft rounded-lg mb-10 text-xs">
        <p class="font-bold text-ink mb-3 font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-[10px]">Table of Contents</p>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-link">
          <li><a href="#short-answer" class="hover:underline">Short Answer — Is It Taxable?</a></li>
          <li><a href="#irs-rule" class="hover:underline">The IRS Rule Under Section 104</a></li>
          <li><a href="#not-taxable" class="hover:underline">What Parts of a Settlement Are NOT Taxable</a></li>
          <li><a href="#taxable" class="hover:underline">What Parts of a Settlement MAY Be Taxable</a></li>
          <li><a href="#lost-wages" class="hover:underline">Special Case: Lost Wages and Tax</a></li>
          <li><a href="#structured" class="hover:underline">Structured Settlements and Tax</a></li>
          <li><a href="#reporting" class="hover:underline">How to Report (or Not Report) Your Settlement</a></li>
          <li><a href="#attorney-fees" class="hover:underline">What About Attorney Fees?</a></li>
